Split of authorship
-------------------

Upstream (c) 2026 drscrewdriver, MIT — the plugin host wiring, the client UI
half (model-panel card, effort slider, family tab, context ring), the
settings/volatile-config plumbing, the session projection scaffolding, the
billing/pricing helpers, and the build layout.

Added or substantially rewritten in this fork (c) 2026 lion231226:

  * difficulty classification from the current user prompt
    (src/difficulty.ts — length buckets, keyword classes, structural signals,
    difficulty bands, difficulty-to-effort mapping);
  * turn isolation of tool samples (per-turn window instead of a session-wide
    ring buffer);
  * a safety-directed fallback (projection or parse failure falls back to
    `high`, configurable through `safeFallback`);
  * nearest-lower clamping for the auto path (never "jump to the highest
    advertised level");
  * decision hysteresis (`hysteresisSteps`) so consecutive identical decisions
    are required before the wire level moves;
  * Windows tool-name coverage in the simple-tool matcher (`pwsh`, `shell`,
    `powershell`, `apply_patch`);
  * preservation of custom wire ids selected by the user (e.g. `ultra`);
  * explainable decisions: every scheduling decision records `reasons[]`.

